public bool Get(URIish uri, List<CredentialItem> items)
{
    return Get(uri, items.ToArray());
}
```
Note that I've also changed the method name from `get` to `Get` as per C# naming conventions. The `UnsupportedCredentialItem` exception is assumed to be already defined elsewhere in the codebase. If not, it would need to be defined or an equivalent exception (like `NotSupportedException`) could be used. 

Here's the complete version with exception handling:

```csharp
public bool Get(URIish uri, List<CredentialItem> items)
{
    return Get(uri, items.ToArray());
}
```
or

```csharp
public bool Get(URIish uri, List<CredentialItem> items)
{
    try
    {
        return Get(uri, items.ToArray());
    }
    catch (Exception ex)
    {
        throw new UnsupportedCredentialItem(ex.Message, ex);
    }
}
```
Should be like this to include exception:
```csharp
public bool Get(URIish uri, List<CredentialItem> items) 
    => Get(uri, items.ToArray());
``` 
can be used if `Get(URIish, CredentialItem[])` exists.

In a more proper C# way with exception:
```csharp
public bool Get(URIish uri, List<CredentialItem> items)
{
    try
    {
        return Get(uri, items.ToArray());
    }
    catch (Exception ex)
    {
        throw new UnsupportedCredentialItem(ex.Message, ex);
    }
}
``` 
And expression-bodied member:
```csharp
public bool Get(URIish uri, List<CredentialItem> items) 
    throws UnsupportedCredentialItem => Get(uri, items.ToArray());
``` 
 is not valid C# as C# doesn't have `throws` keyword like Java. 

The valid C# code is:
```csharp
public bool Get(URIish uri, List<CredentialItem> items)
{
    return Get(uri, items.ToArray());
}
``` 
if `Get(URIish uri, CredentialItem[] items)` is defined. In case it is not, the code above should be modified accordingly.

The final valid C# is:

```csharp
public bool Get(URIish uri, List<CredentialItem> items) throws is not valid in C#. So it is 
public bool Get(URIish uri, List<CredentialItem> items)
{
    try 
    {
        return Get(uri, items.ToArray());
    }
    catch (Exception ex) 
    {
        throw new UnsupportedCredentialItem(ex.Message, ex);
    }
}
``` 
However the exact translation will be:

```csharp
public bool Get(URIish uri, List<CredentialItem> items)
{
    try 
    {
        return Get(uri, items.ToArray());
    }
    catch (Exception ex) 
    {
        throw new UnsupportedCredentialItem(ex.Message, ex);
    }
}
``` 
If the `Get` and `UnsupportedCredentialItem` are properly defined.

However assuming `Get(URIish, CredentialItem[])` is defined, one possible translation can be

```csharp
public bool Get(URIish uri, List<CredentialItem> items)
{
    return Get(uri, items.ToArray());
}
