public static long PopIntersect(long[] arr1, long[] arr2, int wordOffset, int numWords) 
{
    long popCount = 0;
    for (int i = wordOffset, end = wordOffset + numWords; i < end; ++i) 
    {
        popCount += BitOperations.PopCount((ulong)arr1[i] & (ulong)arr2[i]);
    }
    return popCount;
}
```
Note that C# does not have a direct equivalent of `Long.bitCount()` in Java. However, you can use `BitOperations.PopCount()` from the `System.Numerics` namespace in .NET 6 and later versions. If you're using an earlier version, you can use the following alternative implementation:

```csharp
public static int PopCount(ulong x) 
{
    x = x - ((x >> 1) & 0x5555555555555555);
    x = (x & 0x3333333333333333) + ((x >> 2) & 0x3333333333333333);
    x = (x + (x >> 4)) & 0x0F0F0F0F0F0F0F0F;
    x = x + (x >> 8);
    x = x + (x >> 16);
    x = x + (x >> 32);
    return (int)x & 0x7F;
}
```

